---
title: Skillet Cheeseburger Pasta
description: Cheeseburger-flavored pasta shells simmered in beef broth and tomato sauce, finished with cheddar and hot dog relish.
tags: [pasta, one-pan]
course: main
icons: [burger-cheese, pan-frying, tomato]
cuisine: American
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Budget Bytes
  url: https://www.budgetbytes.com/skillet-cheeseburger-pasta/
servings: 4
prep time: 10m
cook time: 25m
---

Finely dice the @yellow onion{1}.

Add the @olive oil{1%tbsp}, onion, and @lean ground beef{1/2%lb} to a large deep #skillet{} and sauté over medium heat until the beef is fully browned and the onion is soft and transparent. Drain off any excess fat, if needed.

Add the @all-purpose flour{2%tbsp} to the skillet and continue to stir and cook for ~cook{1%minute} more. The flour will form a paste that may coat the bottom of the skillet. Be careful not to let the flour burn.

Add the @tomato sauce{1%can}(8 oz), @beef broth{2%cup}, and @pasta shells{1/2%lb}(uncooked) to the skillet. Stir to combine the ingredients and dissolve any of the flour off the bottom of the skillet.

Place a #lid{} on the skillet, turn the heat up to medium-high, and let the liquid come up to a boil. Once it reaches a boil, give it a quick stir, replace the lid, and turn the heat down to medium-low. Let the pasta simmer, stirring occasionally, for ~simmer{10-12%minutes}, or until the pasta is tender and the sauce has thickened. Turn the heat off.

Add the @sharp cheddar{113%g}(4 oz, shredded), a handful at a time, and stir until it has melted into the sauce.

Stir the @hot dog relish{2%tbsp} into the sauce and then top with the @?scallions{2}(sliced). Serve hot.
